{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"A qualifying U.S. in-kind ETF generally remains subject to Rule 22e-4’s **liquidity risk management program**: written policies and procedures, liquidity-risk assessment and periodic review, board oversight, and recordkeeping. It must still manage risks that could impair its ability to meet redemptions, including cash redemptions and other liquidity needs.\n\nRelief is limited: the ETF need not **classify each portfolio investment into the four liquidity categories** (highly liquid, moderately liquid, less liquid, illiquid), nor comply with the related **minimum highly liquid investment requirement (HLIM)** and its shortfall procedures/reporting. This is not a blanket exemption from Rule 22e-4 or from other applicable ETF obligations."}}
